1
00:00:01,220 --> 00:00:02,220
Chapter 20.

2
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:07,059
I had forgotten to draw my curtain, which I

3
00:00:07,059 --> 00:00:10,400
usually did, and also to let down my window blind.

4
00:00:11,529 --> 00:00:16,800
The consequence was that when the moon, which was full and bright for the night

5
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:22,139
was fine, came in her course to that space in the sky opposite my casement,

6
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:28,980
and looked in at me, through the unveiled pains, her glorious gaze roused me.

7
00:00:29,879 --> 00:00:32,953
Awaking in the dead of night, I opened my eyes

8
00:00:32,953 --> 00:00:36,821
on her disc, silver white and crystal clear.

9
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:39,220
It was beautiful, but too solemn.

10
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:43,260
I half rose and stretched my arm to draw the curtain.

11
00:00:43,724 --> 00:00:45,040
Good God, what a cry!

12
00:00:45,989 --> 00:00:50,860
The night, its silence, its rest, was rent in twain by a savage,

13
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:55,000
a sharp, a shrilly sound that ran from end to end of Thornfield Hall.

14
00:00:55,839 --> 00:00:56,839
My pulse stopped.

15
00:00:57,540 --> 00:00:59,239
My heart stood still.

16
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:01,599
My stretched arm was paralyzed.

17
00:01:02,830 --> 00:01:05,239
The cry died and was not renewed.

18
00:01:06,305 --> 00:01:11,160
Indeed, whatever being uttered that fearful shriek could not soon repeat it,

19
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:15,269
not the widest winged condor on the Andes could twice in

20
00:01:15,269 --> 00:01:20,120
succession, send out such a yell from the cloud shrouding his airy.

21
00:01:21,129 --> 00:01:26,080
The thing delivering such utterance must rest air it could repeat the effort.

22
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:34,900
It came out of the third story for it passed overhead, and overhead, yes.

23
00:01:35,019 --> 00:01:39,980
In the room just above my chamber ceiling, I now heard a struggle, a deadly one it

24
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:44,599
seemed from the noise, and a half -smothered voice shouted, help,

25
00:01:45,059 --> 00:01:47,879
help, help, three times rapidly.

26
00:01:48,519 --> 00:01:50,760
Well, no one come, it cried.

27
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:56,040
And then, while the staggering and stamping went on wildly, I distinguished

28
00:01:56,040 --> 00:02:02,540
through plank and plaster, rochester, rochester, for God's sake, come!

29
00:02:04,019 --> 00:02:10,599
A chamber door opened, someone ran or rushed along the gallery, another step

30
00:02:10,601 --> 00:02:14,500
stamped on the flooring above and something fell, and there was silence.

31
00:02:15,779 --> 00:02:19,224
I had put on some clothes, though horror shook

32
00:02:19,224 --> 00:02:22,601
all my limbs, I issued from my apartment.

33
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:30,120
The sleepers were all aroused, ejaculations, terrified murmurs sounded in every room.

34
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:37,201
Door after door unclosed, one looked out and another looked out, the gallery filled.

35
00:02:37,919 --> 00:02:42,779
Gentlemen and ladies alike had quitted their beds and, oh, what is it?

36
00:02:43,199 --> 00:02:44,199
Who is hurt?

37
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:45,660
What has happened?

38
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:47,580
Fetch a light.

39
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:49,040
Is it fire?

40
00:02:49,339 --> 00:02:50,339
Are there robbers?

41
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:51,760
Where shall we run?

42
00:02:52,599 --> 00:02:56,091
Was demanded confusedly on all hands, but for the

43
00:02:56,091 --> 00:02:59,739
moonlight they would have been in complete darkness.

44
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:05,839
They ran to and fro, they crowded together, some sobbed, some stumbled,

45
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:08,419
the confusion was inextricable.

46
00:03:09,639 --> 00:03:15,701
Where the devil is rochester, cried Colonel Dent, I cannot find him in his bed.

47
00:03:15,819 --> 00:03:18,839
Here, here was shouted in return.

48
00:03:19,660 --> 00:03:21,940
Be composed all of you, I'm coming.

49
00:03:22,559 --> 00:03:25,625
And the door at the end of the gallery opened,

50
00:03:25,627 --> 00:03:29,141
and Mr. Rochester advanced with a candle.

51
00:03:29,279 --> 00:03:31,580
He had just descended from the upper story.

52
00:03:32,660 --> 00:03:38,059
One of the ladies ran to him directly, she seized his arm, it was Miss Ingram.

53
00:03:39,580 --> 00:03:42,980
What awful event has taken place, said she.

54
00:03:43,639 --> 00:03:44,639
Speak.

55
00:03:44,959 --> 00:03:46,580
Let us know the worst at once.

56
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:50,300
But don't pull me down or strangle me, he replied.

57
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,220
For the Mrs. Eshton were clinging about him now.

58
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:57,855
And the two Dowagers, in vast white wrappers,

59
00:03:57,855 --> 00:04:01,559
were bearing down on him like ships in full sail.

60
00:04:03,019 --> 00:04:05,680
All's right, all's right, he cried.

61
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:08,739
It's a mere rehearsal of much ado about nothing.

62
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:13,220
Ladies, keep off, or I shall wax dangerous.

63
00:04:14,180 --> 00:04:17,161
And dangerous, he looked, his black eyes dotted

64
00:04:17,163 --> 00:04:20,000
sparks, calming himself by an effort he added.

65
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:23,860
A servant has had the nightmare, that is all.

66
00:04:24,599 --> 00:04:27,120
She's an excitable nervous person.

67
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:31,919
She can strewd her dream into an apparition, or something of that sort,

68
00:04:32,239 --> 00:04:35,379
no doubt, and has taken a fit with fright.

69
00:04:36,559 --> 00:04:39,839
Now then, I must see you all back into your rooms.

70
00:04:40,639 --> 00:04:43,940
For till the house is settled, she cannot be looked after.

71
00:04:45,019 --> 00:04:48,680
Gentlemen, have the goodness to set the ladies the example.

72
00:04:49,459 --> 00:04:55,239
Miss Ingram, I am sure you will not fail in convincing superiority to idle terrors.

73
00:04:56,160 --> 00:05:01,059
Ami and Luisa, return to your nests like a pair of doves as you are.

74
00:05:02,019 --> 00:05:04,000
May dam to the Dowagers.

75
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:09,419
You will take cold to a dead certainty if you stay in this chill gallery any longer.

76
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:16,459
And so, by dint of alternate coaxing and commanding, he can try to get them all

77
00:05:16,461 --> 00:05:19,139
once more enclosed in their separate dormitories.

78
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:22,400
I did not wait to be ordered back to mine.

79
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:27,139
But retreated unnoticed, as unnoticed I had left it.

80
00:05:27,739 --> 00:05:30,019
Not, however, to go to bed.

81
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:34,139
On the contrary, I began and dressed myself carefully.

82
00:05:35,279 --> 00:05:40,220
The sounds I had heard after the scream, and the words that had been uttered,

83
00:05:40,580 --> 00:05:43,139
had probably been heard only by me.

84
00:05:44,080 --> 00:05:46,980
For they had proceeded from the room above mine.

85
00:05:47,819 --> 00:05:52,339
But they assured me that it was not a servant stream which had thus struck

86
00:05:52,341 --> 00:05:58,040
horror through the house, and that the explanation Mr. Rochester had given was

87
00:05:58,040 --> 00:06:01,639
merely an invention framed to pacify his guests.

88
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:05,720
I dressed then to be ready for emergencies.

89
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:12,040
When dressed, I sat a long time by the window looking out over the silent grounds

90
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:16,379
and silvid fields, and waiting for I knew not what.

91
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:24,239
It seemed to me that some event must follow the strange cry, struggle and call.

92
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:28,559
No, stillness returned.

93
00:06:29,559 --> 00:06:33,362
Each murmur and movement ceased gradually, and in about

94
00:06:33,364 --> 00:06:37,019
an hour, Thornfield Hall was again as hushed as a desert.

95
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:41,319
It seemed that sleep and night had resumed their empire.

96
00:06:42,379 --> 00:06:43,879
Meantime, the moon declined.

97
00:06:44,819 --> 00:06:45,819
She was about to set.

98
00:06:46,839 --> 00:06:49,497
Not liking to sit in the cold and darkness, I

99
00:06:49,497 --> 00:06:52,599
thought I would lie down on my bed dressed as I was.

100
00:06:53,419 --> 00:06:59,300
I left the window, and moved with little noise across the carpet, as I stooped to

101
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:03,279
take off my shoes, a cautious hand tapped low at the door.

102
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:05,500
Am I wanted?

103
00:07:05,940 --> 00:07:06,360
I asked.

104
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:07,760
Are you up?

105
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:09,180
Ask the voice I expected to hear.

106
00:07:09,339 --> 00:07:10,360
Viz, my masters.

107
00:07:11,319 --> 00:07:12,319
Yes, sir.

108
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:13,440
And dressed.

109
00:07:13,879 --> 00:07:14,879
Yes.

110
00:07:15,059 --> 00:07:16,260
Come out then, quietly.

111
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:18,300
I obeyed.

112
00:07:18,699 --> 00:07:21,199
Mr. Rochester stood in the gallery holding a light.

113
00:07:21,879 --> 00:07:23,440
I want you, he said.

114
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:25,300
Come this way.

115
00:07:25,580 --> 00:07:27,500
Take your time and make no noise.

116
00:07:28,819 --> 00:07:29,900
My slippers were thin.

117
00:07:30,839 --> 00:07:33,959
I could walk the matted floor as softly as a cat.

118
00:07:34,959 --> 00:07:39,040
He glided up the gallery and up the stairs, and stopped in the dark,

119
00:07:39,379 --> 00:07:41,879
low corridor of the fateful third story.

120
00:07:42,739 --> 00:07:45,120
I had followed and stood at his side.

121
00:07:46,639 --> 00:07:47,919
Have you a sponge in your room?

122
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:49,500
He asked in a whisper.

123
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,040
Yes, sir.

124
00:07:51,779 --> 00:07:52,779
Have you any salts?

125
00:07:52,959 --> 00:07:53,959
Volatile salts?

126
00:07:54,419 --> 00:07:55,419
Yes.

127
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:57,180
Go back and fetch both.

128
00:07:58,360 --> 00:08:02,580
I returned, sought the sponge on the washstand, the salts in my drawer,

129
00:08:03,319 --> 00:08:05,419
and once more retraced my steps.

130
00:08:06,099 --> 00:08:07,099
He still waited.

131
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:12,099
He held a key in his hand, approaching one of the small black doors.

132
00:08:12,739 --> 00:08:13,739
He put it in the lock.

133
00:08:14,379 --> 00:08:16,540
He paused and addressed me again.

134
00:08:17,339 --> 00:08:19,019
You don't turn sick at the sight of blood?

135
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:21,220
I think I shall not.

136
00:08:22,099 --> 00:08:23,639
I have never been tried yet.

137
00:08:24,959 --> 00:08:29,639
I felt a thrill while I answered him, but no coldness and no faintness.

138
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:33,019
Just give me your hand, he said.

139
00:08:33,660 --> 00:08:35,660
It will not do to risk a fainting fit.

140
00:08:36,819 --> 00:08:38,220
I put my fingers into his.

141
00:08:39,660 --> 00:08:42,120
Warm and steady was his remark.

142
00:08:43,059 --> 00:08:44,779
He turned the key and opened the door.

143
00:08:45,980 --> 00:08:48,519
I saw a room I remembered to have seen before.

144
00:08:49,559 --> 00:08:51,839
The day Mrs. Fairfax showed me over the house.

145
00:08:52,819 --> 00:08:54,040
It was hung with tapestry.

146
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:59,760
But the tapestry was now looped up in one part, and there was a door apparent,

147
00:09:00,459 --> 00:09:01,720
which had then been concealed.

148
00:09:02,680 --> 00:09:04,239
This door was open.

149
00:09:04,980 --> 00:09:07,239
A light shone out of the room within.

150
00:09:07,940 --> 00:09:12,839
I heard thenc a snarling, snatching sound, almost like a dog quarreling.

151
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:19,438
Mr. Rochester, putting down his candle, said to me, wait

152
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:22,720
a minute, and he went forward to the inner apartment.

153
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:29,339
A shout of laughter greeted his entrance, noisy at first, and terminating in

154
00:09:29,341 --> 00:09:34,360
Gracepool's own goblin, haha, she then was there.

155
00:09:35,599 --> 00:09:37,898
He made some sort of arrangement without

156
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:41,161
speaking, though I heard a low voice address him.

157
00:09:41,620 --> 00:09:43,819
He came out and closed the door behind him.

158
00:09:45,239 --> 00:09:50,300
Here Jane, he said, and I walked round to the other side of a large bed,

159
00:09:50,839 --> 00:09:56,360
which, with its drawn curtains, concealed a considerable portion of the chamber.

160
00:09:56,559 --> 00:09:58,220
An easy chair was near the bedhead.

161
00:09:58,980 --> 00:10:02,300
A man sat in it, dressed with the exception of his coat.

162
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:04,120
He was still.

163
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:06,180
His head lent back.

164
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:07,940
His eyes were closed.

165
00:10:08,839 --> 00:10:10,739
Mr. Rochester held the candle over him.

166
00:10:11,419 --> 00:10:16,480
I recognized in his pale and seemingly lifeless face, the stranger Mason.

167
00:10:17,260 --> 00:10:22,120
I saw, too, that his linen on one side and one arm was almost soaked in blood.

168
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:27,860
Hold the candle, said Mr. Rochester, and I took it.

169
00:10:28,559 --> 00:10:30,699
He fetched a basin of water from the washstand.

170
00:10:31,260 --> 00:10:33,720
Hold that, said he, I obeyed.

171
00:10:34,260 --> 00:10:38,860
He took the sponge, dipped it in, and moistened the corpse-like face.

172
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:43,660
He asked for my smelling bottle and applied it to the nostrils.

173
00:10:44,819 --> 00:10:47,220
Mr. Mason shortly unclosed his eyes.

174
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:49,080
He groaned.

175
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:52,629
Mr. Rochester opened the shirt of the wounded

176
00:10:52,629 --> 00:10:55,781
man, whose arm and shoulder were bandaged.

177
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:58,599
He spunged away blood, trickling fast down.

178
00:10:59,959 --> 00:11:01,980
Is there immediate danger?

179
00:11:02,819 --> 00:11:03,940
Mermaid, Mr. Mason.

180
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,680
Poo, no, I'm your scratch.

181
00:11:07,620 --> 00:11:09,319
Don't be so overcome, man, bear up.

182
00:11:09,919 --> 00:11:11,519
I'll fetch a surgeon for you now myself.

183
00:11:12,099 --> 00:11:13,980
You'll be able to be removed by morning, I hope.

184
00:11:14,699 --> 00:11:15,959
Jane, he continued.

185
00:11:16,599 --> 00:11:22,339
Sir, I shall have to leave you in this room with this gentleman for an hour,

186
00:11:22,699 --> 00:11:23,860
or perhaps two hours.

187
00:11:24,839 --> 00:11:27,860
You will sponge the blood as I do when it returns.

188
00:11:28,660 --> 00:11:32,368
If he feels faint, you will put the glass of water

189
00:11:32,370 --> 00:11:35,699
on that stand to his lips and your salts to his nose.

190
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:43,000
You will not speak to him on any pretext, and, Richard, it will be at the peril of

191
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:48,040
your life if you speak to her, open your lips, agitate yourself,

192
00:11:48,519 --> 00:11:50,540
and I'll not answer for the consequences.

193
00:11:52,279 --> 00:11:54,400
Again, the poor man groaned.

194
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:56,919
He looked as if he dared not move.

195
00:11:57,519 --> 00:12:03,019
Fear, either of death or of something else, appeared almost to paralyze him.

196
00:12:04,239 --> 00:12:07,345
Mr. Rochester put the now bloody sponge into my

197
00:12:07,345 --> 00:12:10,701
hand, and I proceeded to use it as he had done.

198
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:18,120
He watched me a second, then saying, remember no conversation he left the room.

199
00:12:19,339 --> 00:12:22,821
I experienced a strange feeling as the key graded in the

200
00:12:22,822 --> 00:12:26,980
lock, and the sound of his retreating step ceased to be heard.

201
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:32,879
Here, then, I was in the third story, fastened into one of its mystic cells,

202
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:38,540
night around me, a pale and bloody spectacle under my eyes and hands,

203
00:12:39,199 --> 00:12:42,779
a murderous, hardly separated from me by a single door.

204
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:46,599
Yes, that was appalling the rest I could bear.

205
00:12:47,519 --> 00:12:52,080
But I shuddered at the thought of grace pool bursting out upon me.

206
00:12:53,519 --> 00:12:56,120
I must keep to my post, however.

207
00:12:57,279 --> 00:12:59,860
I must watch this ghastly countenance.

208
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:03,660
These blue still lips forbidden to unclose.

209
00:13:04,559 --> 00:13:08,419
These eyes now shut, now opening, now wandering through the room,

210
00:13:08,540 --> 00:13:12,860
now fixing on me, and ever glazed with the dullness of horror.

211
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:17,660
I must dip my hand again and again in the basin of

212
00:13:17,661 --> 00:13:21,059
blood and water, and wipe away the trickling gaw.

213
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:26,620
I must see the light of the unsnuffed candle wane on my employment.

214
00:13:27,459 --> 00:13:33,620
The shadows darken on the wrought, antique tapestry round me, and grow black

215
00:13:33,620 --> 00:13:37,266
under the hangings of the vast old bed, and quiver

216
00:13:37,266 --> 00:13:40,879
strangely over the doors of a great cabinet opposite.

217
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:48,639
Whose front, divided into twelve panels, bore in grim design, the heads of the

218
00:13:48,641 --> 00:13:53,339
twelve apostles, each enclosed in its separate panel as in a frame.

219
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:59,599
While above them, at the top, rose an ebb and crucifix and a dying Christ.

220
00:14:00,879 --> 00:14:05,599
According as the shifting obscurity and flickering gleam hoved here or glanced

221
00:14:05,601 --> 00:14:10,519
there, it was now the bearded physician, Luke, that bent his brow.

222
00:14:11,419 --> 00:14:17,620
Now Syngin's long hair that waived, and a non, the devilish face of Judas,

223
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:22,720
that grew out of the panel, and seemed gathering life and threatening a

224
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:27,839
revelation of the arch-trater of Satan himself in his subordinate's form.

225
00:14:29,040 --> 00:14:34,339
Amidst all this, I had to listen as well as watch, to listen for the movements of

226
00:14:34,341 --> 00:14:37,160
the wild beast or the fiend in Yonder's side, Den.

227
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:42,919
But since Mr. Rochester's visit, it seemed spellbound.

228
00:14:43,599 --> 00:14:48,919
All the night, I heard but three sounds at three long intervals, a step creek,

229
00:14:49,379 --> 00:14:54,260
a momentary renewal of the snarling canine noise, and a deep human groan.

230
00:14:54,980 --> 00:14:57,779
Then, my own thoughts worried me.

231
00:14:58,620 --> 00:15:04,300
What crime was this, that lived incarnate in the sequestered mansion, and could

232
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:07,019
neither be expelled nor subdued by the owner?

233
00:15:07,919 --> 00:15:10,811
What mystery, that broke out now in fire and

234
00:15:10,811 --> 00:15:14,580
now in blood at the deadest hours of night?

235
00:15:15,300 --> 00:15:20,480
What creature was it, that masked in an ordinary woman's face and shape,

236
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:24,228
uttered the voice, now of a mocking demon,

237
00:15:24,230 --> 00:15:27,379
and a non of a carry on seeking bird of prey?

238
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:32,860
And this man, I bent over, this commonplace quiet stranger.

239
00:15:33,660 --> 00:15:36,000
How had he become involved in the web of horror?

240
00:15:36,900 --> 00:15:39,120
And why had the fury flown at him?

241
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:43,264
What made him seek this quarter of the house at an

242
00:15:43,266 --> 00:15:45,919
untimely season, when he should have been asleep in bed?

243
00:15:47,459 --> 00:15:50,860
I had heard Mr. Rochester assign him an apartment below.

244
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:52,860
What brought him here?

245
00:15:53,900 --> 00:15:59,459
And why, now, was he so tame under the violence or treachery done him?

246
00:16:00,379 --> 00:16:05,000
Why did he so quietly submit to the concealment, Mr. Rochester enforced?

247
00:16:05,919 --> 00:16:09,019
Why did Mr. Rochester enforce this concealment?

248
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:11,720
His guest had been outraged.

249
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:17,120
His own life on a former occasion had been hideously plotted against, and both

250
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:21,059
attempts he smothered in secrecy and sank in oblivion.

251
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:29,779
Lastly, I saw Mr. Mason was submissive to Mr. Rochester, that the impetuous will of

252
00:16:29,781 --> 00:16:33,980
the latter held complete sway over the inertness of the former.

253
00:16:34,940 --> 00:16:39,680
The few words which had passed between them assured me of this.

254
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:47,080
It was evident that in their former intercourse, the passive disposition of

255
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:52,040
the one had been habitually influenced by the active energy of the other.

256
00:16:53,739 --> 00:16:59,680
Once then had arisen, Mr. Rochester's dismay, when he heard of Mr.

257
00:16:59,680 --> 00:17:01,421
Mason's arrival.

258
00:17:01,860 --> 00:17:07,019
Why had the mere name of this unresisting individual, whom his word now suffice to

259
00:17:07,021 --> 00:17:10,499
control like child, fallen on him, a few hours

260
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:13,561
since as a thunderbolt might fall on an oak?

261
00:17:14,319 --> 00:17:20,239
Oh, I could not forget his look and his paleness when he whispered, Jane,

262
00:17:20,819 --> 00:17:24,360
I have got a blow, I have got a blow, Jane.

263
00:17:25,220 --> 00:17:29,620
I could not forget how the arm had trembled, which he rested on my shoulder.

264
00:17:30,379 --> 00:17:34,218
And it was no light matter, which could thus bow the resolute

265
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:38,319
spirit and thrill the vigorous frame of Fairfax Rochester.

266
00:17:39,419 --> 00:17:40,900
When will he come?

267
00:17:41,639 --> 00:17:43,160
When will he come?

268
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:49,519
I cried inwardly, as the night lingered and lingered, as my bleeding patient

269
00:17:49,521 --> 00:17:54,440
drooped, moaned, sickened, and neither day nor aid arrived.

270
00:17:55,379 --> 00:17:59,781
I had again and again held the water to Mason's white

271
00:17:59,783 --> 00:18:03,139
lips, again and again offered him the stimulating salts.

272
00:18:03,739 --> 00:18:05,540
My efforts seemed ineffectual.

273
00:18:06,260 --> 00:18:09,739
Either bodily or mental suffering or loss of blood or

274
00:18:09,741 --> 00:18:12,860
all three combined were fast -prostrating his strength.

275
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:17,940
He moaned so, and looked so weak, wild, and lost.

276
00:18:18,580 --> 00:18:22,139
I feared he was dying, and I might not even speak to him.

277
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:26,319
The candle wasted at last, went out.

278
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:31,940
As it expired, I perceived streaks of gray light edging the window curtains.

279
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:33,879
Dawn was then approaching.

280
00:18:34,779 --> 00:18:40,480
Presently, I heard pilot bark far below, out of his distant kennel in the courtyard.

281
00:18:40,639 --> 00:18:41,639
Hope revived.

282
00:18:42,639 --> 00:18:44,279
Nor was it unwarranted.

283
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,968
In five minutes more, the grating key, the

284
00:18:47,970 --> 00:18:51,741
yielding lock warned me my watch was relieved.

285
00:18:51,940 --> 00:18:53,760
It could not have lasted more than two hours.

286
00:18:54,459 --> 00:18:55,959
Many a week has seemed shorter.

287
00:18:57,239 --> 00:18:58,599
Mr. Rochester entered.

288
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:01,839
And with him, the surgeon he had been to fetch.

289
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:06,620
Now Carter, beyond the alert, he said to this last.

290
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:12,080
I give you but half an hour for dressing the wound, fastening the bandages,

291
00:19:12,879 --> 00:19:14,720
getting the patient downstairs and all.

292
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,760
But is he fit to move, sir?

293
00:19:19,199 --> 00:19:20,319
No doubt of it.

294
00:19:20,699 --> 00:19:21,699
It is nothing serious.

295
00:19:21,819 --> 00:19:22,500
He is nervous.

296
00:19:22,699 --> 00:19:24,080
His spirits must be kept up.

297
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:26,180
Come, set to work.

298
00:19:27,699 --> 00:19:35,379
Mr. Rochester drew back the thick curtain, drew up the Holland blind, let in all the

299
00:19:35,381 --> 00:19:41,940
daylight he could, and I was surprised and cheered to see how far Dawn was advanced,

300
00:19:42,459 --> 00:19:45,559
what rosy streaks were beginning to brighten the east.

301
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:51,099
Then he approached Mason, whom the surgeon was already handling.

302
00:19:52,739 --> 00:19:54,819
Now, my good fellow, how are you?

303
00:19:55,319 --> 00:19:56,319
He asked.

304
00:19:56,540 --> 00:19:59,019
She's done for me, I fear, was the faint reply.

305
00:19:59,839 --> 00:20:01,480
Not a wit, courage.

306
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:05,819
This day, fortnight, you'll hardly be a pin the worse of it.

307
00:20:06,500 --> 00:20:08,160
You've lost a little blood, that's all.

308
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:11,959
Carter assured him there's no danger.

309
00:20:13,419 --> 00:20:15,319
I can do that conscientiously.

310
00:20:15,940 --> 00:20:19,059
Said Carter, who had now undone the bandages.

311
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:22,519
Only, I wish I could have got here sooner.

312
00:20:23,220 --> 00:20:24,760
He would not have bled so much.

313
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:26,400
But how is this?

314
00:20:26,940 --> 00:20:29,559
The flesh on the shoulder is torn as well as cut.

315
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:32,059
This wound was not done with a knife.

316
00:20:32,919 --> 00:20:34,180
There have been teeth here.

317
00:20:35,879 --> 00:20:36,879
She bit me.

318
00:20:37,660 --> 00:20:38,660
He murmured.

319
00:20:38,940 --> 00:20:42,660
She worried me like a tiger's when Rochester got the knife from her.

320
00:20:43,419 --> 00:20:44,980
You should not have yielded.

321
00:20:45,500 --> 00:20:48,860
You should have grappled with her at once, said Mr. Rochester.

322
00:20:50,260 --> 00:20:53,419
But under such circumstances, what could one do?

323
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:55,220
Returned Mason.

324
00:20:56,080 --> 00:20:59,660
Oh, it was frightful, he added, shuddering.

325
00:21:00,419 --> 00:21:02,379
And I did not expect it.

326
00:21:03,120 --> 00:21:04,940
She looked so quiet at first.

327
00:21:05,739 --> 00:21:08,699
I warned you, was his friend's answer.

328
00:21:09,760 --> 00:21:12,739
I said, be on your guard when you go near her.

329
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:17,080
Besides, you might have waited till tomorrow and had me with you.

330
00:21:17,639 --> 00:21:21,339
It was mere folly to attempt the interview tonight, and alone.

331
00:21:23,720 --> 00:21:26,199
I thought I could have done some good.

332
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:33,080
You thought, you thought, yes, it makes me impatient to hear you.

333
00:21:33,919 --> 00:21:36,872
But however you have suffered, and are likely

334
00:21:36,874 --> 00:21:39,500
to suffer enough for not taking my advice.

335
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:42,339
So I'll say no more.

336
00:21:43,120 --> 00:21:48,360
Carter, hurry, hurry, the sun will soon rise, and I must have him off.

337
00:21:49,760 --> 00:21:52,500
Directly sir, the shoulder is just bandaged.

338
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:55,620
I must look to this other wound in the arm.

339
00:21:56,239 --> 00:21:57,940
She has had a teeth here too, I think.

340
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:00,000
She sucked the blood.

341
00:22:00,680 --> 00:22:03,620
She said she drained my heart, said Mason.

342
00:22:05,019 --> 00:22:06,779
I saw Mr. Rochester's shudder.

343
00:22:07,760 --> 00:22:13,720
A singularly marked expression of disgust, horror, hatred, warped his countenance

344
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:18,440
almost to distortion, but he only said, come, be silent,

345
00:22:18,442 --> 00:22:22,379
Richard, and never mind her gibberish, don't repeat it.

346
00:22:23,279 --> 00:22:26,180
I wish I could forget it was the answer.

347
00:22:27,459 --> 00:22:32,580
You will, when you are out of the country, when you get back to Spanish town,

348
00:22:33,220 --> 00:22:39,661
you may think of her as dead and buried, or rather, you need not think of her at all.

349
00:22:40,660 --> 00:22:42,360
Impossible to forget this night.

350
00:22:43,519 --> 00:22:45,040
It is not impossible.

351
00:22:45,739 --> 00:22:46,959
Have some energy man.

352
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:50,527
You thought you were as dead as a herring two

353
00:22:50,529 --> 00:22:53,860
hours since, and you are all alive and talking now.

354
00:22:54,639 --> 00:22:57,940
There, Carter has done with you or nearly so.

355
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:01,800
I'll make you decent in a trice, Jane.

356
00:23:03,220 --> 00:23:05,860
He turned to me for the first time since his re-entrance.

357
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:09,709
Take this key, go down into my bedroom, and

358
00:23:09,711 --> 00:23:13,760
walk straight forward into my dressing room.

359
00:23:14,019 --> 00:23:17,559
Open the top drawer of the wardrobe, and take out a clean shirt and neck

360
00:23:17,561 --> 00:23:21,099
hankerchief, bring them here, and be nimble.

361
00:23:22,540 --> 00:23:28,440
I went, sought the repository he had mentioned, found the articles named,

362
00:23:29,059 --> 00:23:30,099
and returned with them.

363
00:23:31,059 --> 00:23:34,451
Now, said he, go to the other side of the bed

364
00:23:34,451 --> 00:23:38,000
while I order his toilet, but don't leave the room.

365
00:23:38,300 --> 00:23:39,379
You may be wanted again.

366
00:23:40,319 --> 00:23:42,220
I retired as directed.

367
00:23:43,500 --> 00:23:47,184
Was anybody stirring below when you went down, Jane, inquired Mr.

368
00:23:47,184 --> 00:23:48,800
Rochester presently?

369
00:23:49,739 --> 00:23:50,739
No sir.

370
00:23:51,379 --> 00:23:53,059
All was very still.

371
00:23:54,660 --> 00:24:00,540
We shall get you off cannelly dick, and it will be better, both for your sake,

372
00:24:01,160 --> 00:24:03,160
and for that of the poor creature in Yonder.

373
00:24:03,839 --> 00:24:08,919
I have striven long to avoid exposure, and I should not like it to come at last.

374
00:24:10,639 --> 00:24:13,680
Here, Carter, help him on with his waste coat.

375
00:24:14,580 --> 00:24:16,260
Where did you leave your third cloak?

376
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:18,779
You can't travel a mile without that.

377
00:24:18,959 --> 00:24:22,139
I know in this damned cold climate in your room.

378
00:24:23,419 --> 00:24:26,201
Jane, run down to Mr. Mason's room, the one

379
00:24:26,201 --> 00:24:29,281
next mine, and fetch a cloak you will see there.

380
00:24:30,120 --> 00:24:37,061
Again, I ran and again returned, bearing an immense mantle, lined and edged with fur.

381
00:24:37,540 --> 00:24:41,639
Now, I have another errand for you, said my untiring master.

382
00:24:42,540 --> 00:24:44,220
You must away to my room again.

383
00:24:44,980 --> 00:24:47,540
What a mercy you are shod with velvet, Jane.

384
00:24:48,540 --> 00:24:51,459
A clawed hopping messenger would never do at this juncture.

385
00:24:52,239 --> 00:24:54,974
You must open the middle drawer of my toilet table and take

386
00:24:54,976 --> 00:24:57,519
out a little file and a little glass you will find there.

387
00:24:57,940 --> 00:24:58,940
Quick!

388
00:25:00,120 --> 00:25:03,680
I flew, sither and back, bringing the desired vessels.

389
00:25:05,319 --> 00:25:06,319
That's well.

390
00:25:07,080 --> 00:25:09,872
Now, doctor, I shall take the liberty of

391
00:25:09,872 --> 00:25:13,400
administering a dose myself on my own responsibility.

392
00:25:14,360 --> 00:25:20,940
I got this cordial at Rome of an Italian charlatan, a fellow you would have kicked,

393
00:25:21,139 --> 00:25:21,419
Carter.

394
00:25:22,139 --> 00:25:25,360
It is not a thing to be used indiscriminately, but

395
00:25:25,360 --> 00:25:28,540
it is good upon a occasion, as now, for instance.

396
00:25:29,639 --> 00:25:31,360
Jane, a little water.

397
00:25:32,319 --> 00:25:34,883
He held out the tiny glass, and I har filled

398
00:25:34,885 --> 00:25:37,921
it from the water bottle on the washstand.

399
00:25:38,379 --> 00:25:39,379
That will do.

400
00:25:39,919 --> 00:25:41,540
Now wet the lip of the file.

401
00:25:42,379 --> 00:25:43,379
I did so.

402
00:25:43,860 --> 00:25:48,360
He measured 12 drops of a crimson liquid and presented it to Mason.

403
00:25:49,819 --> 00:25:50,819
Drink, Richard.

404
00:25:51,379 --> 00:25:54,000
It will give you the heart you lack for an hour or so.

405
00:25:54,980 --> 00:25:56,339
But will it hurt me?

406
00:25:56,500 --> 00:25:57,900
Is it inflammatory?

407
00:25:58,639 --> 00:25:59,639
Drink, drink, drink.

408
00:26:00,819 --> 00:26:05,839
Mr. Mason obeyed, because it was evidently useless to resist.

409
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:08,099
He was dressed now.

410
00:26:08,919 --> 00:26:13,339
He still looked pale, but he was no longer gory and solid.

411
00:26:14,680 --> 00:26:18,139
Mr. Rochester let him sit three minutes after he had swallowed the liquid.

412
00:26:19,040 --> 00:26:20,319
He then took his arm.

413
00:26:21,160 --> 00:26:25,000
Now I am sure you can get on your feet, he said.

414
00:26:25,559 --> 00:26:26,559
Try.

415
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:27,720
The patient rose.

416
00:26:28,699 --> 00:26:30,760
Carter, take him under the other shoulder.

417
00:26:31,400 --> 00:26:32,415
Be of good cheer, Richard.

418
00:26:32,440 --> 00:26:32,919
Step out.

419
00:26:33,099 --> 00:26:34,099
That's it.

420
00:26:34,660 --> 00:26:35,660
I do feel better.

421
00:26:36,239 --> 00:26:37,239
Remarked, Mr. Mason.

422
00:26:37,980 --> 00:26:38,980
I am sure you do.

423
00:26:39,540 --> 00:26:40,540
Now, Jane.

424
00:26:40,980 --> 00:26:43,099
Trip on before us away to the back stairs.

425
00:26:43,980 --> 00:26:46,773
Unbolt the side-passage door and tell the driver of the

426
00:26:46,775 --> 00:26:50,360
post-shays you will see in the yard, or just outside.

427
00:26:51,099 --> 00:26:54,480
For I told him not to drive his rattling wheels over the pavement.

428
00:26:55,300 --> 00:26:57,961
To be ready, we are coming and Jane, if anyone

429
00:26:57,961 --> 00:27:00,601
is about, come to the foot of the stairs and him.

430
00:27:02,480 --> 00:27:05,419
It was by this time, half past five.

431
00:27:06,099 --> 00:27:08,199
And the sun was on the point of rising.

432
00:27:09,059 --> 00:27:11,660
But I found the kitchen still dark and silent.

433
00:27:12,660 --> 00:27:14,699
The side-passage door was fastened.

434
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:17,620
I opened it with as little noise as possible.

435
00:27:18,379 --> 00:27:19,379
All the yard was quiet.

436
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:21,980
But the gates stood wide open.

437
00:27:22,639 --> 00:27:26,093
And there was a post-shays with horses ready, harnessed,

438
00:27:26,095 --> 00:27:28,739
and drivers seated on the box stationed outside.

439
00:27:29,519 --> 00:27:33,019
I approached him and said the gentleman were coming.

440
00:27:33,940 --> 00:27:34,940
He nodded.

441
00:27:35,739 --> 00:27:39,220
Then I looked carefully round and listened.

442
00:27:40,199 --> 00:27:43,480
The stillness of early morning slumbered everywhere.

443
00:27:44,040 --> 00:27:47,440
The curtains were yet drawn over the servants' chamber windows.

444
00:27:48,379 --> 00:27:52,300
Little birds were just twittering in the blossom-blanched orchard trees,

445
00:27:52,959 --> 00:27:59,061
whose bows drooped like white garlands over the wall and closing one side of the yard.

446
00:27:59,720 --> 00:28:03,940
The carriage horses stamped from time to time in their closed stables.

447
00:28:05,099 --> 00:28:07,220
All else was still.

448
00:28:08,779 --> 00:28:10,239
The gentleman now appeared.

449
00:28:11,199 --> 00:28:13,322
Mason, supported by Mr. Rochester and the

450
00:28:13,324 --> 00:28:16,860
surgeon, seemed to walk with tolerable ease.

451
00:28:16,900 --> 00:28:18,440
They assisted him into the shays.

452
00:28:19,319 --> 00:28:20,379
Carter followed.

453
00:28:21,779 --> 00:28:25,160
Take care of him," said Mr. Rochester to the latter.

454
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:28,339
And keep him at your house till he is quite well.

455
00:28:29,180 --> 00:28:32,199
I shall ride over in a day or two to see how he gets on.

456
00:28:32,919 --> 00:28:35,000
Richard, how is it with you?

457
00:28:36,639 --> 00:28:39,000
The fresh air revives me fair facts.

458
00:28:40,260 --> 00:28:41,959
Leave the window open on his side, Carter.

459
00:28:41,961 --> 00:28:44,400
There is no wind, goodbye dick.

460
00:28:45,360 --> 00:28:46,360
Fair facts?

461
00:28:46,959 --> 00:28:47,959
Well, what is it?

462
00:28:49,040 --> 00:28:53,819
Let her be taken care of, let her be treated as tenderly as maybe, let her,

463
00:28:54,239 --> 00:28:56,220
he stopped and burst into tears.

464
00:28:57,480 --> 00:29:01,599
I do my best and have done it and will do it was the answer.

465
00:29:02,639 --> 00:29:06,059
He shut up the shares door and the vehicle drove away.

466
00:29:07,519 --> 00:29:10,180
Yet, to God, there was an end of all this.

467
00:29:10,819 --> 00:29:14,540
Added Mr. Rochester as he closed and barred the heavy yard gates.

468
00:29:15,059 --> 00:29:19,025
This done, he moved with slow step and abstracted

469
00:29:19,027 --> 00:29:22,419
air towards a door in the wall bordering the orchard.

470
00:29:23,180 --> 00:29:27,639
I, supposing he had done with me, prepared to return to the house.

471
00:29:28,099 --> 00:29:30,940
Again, however, I heard him call Jane.

472
00:29:32,480 --> 00:29:36,500
He had opened the portal and stood at it, waiting for me.

473
00:29:37,800 --> 00:29:39,440
Come where there is some freshness.

474
00:29:40,180 --> 00:29:42,139
For a few moments, he said.

475
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:44,419
That house is a mere dungeon.

476
00:29:45,279 --> 00:29:46,279
Don't you feel it so?

477
00:29:47,300 --> 00:29:49,860
It seems to me a splendid mansion, sir.

478
00:29:51,199 --> 00:29:55,019
The glamour of inexperience is over your eyes, he answered.

479
00:29:55,739 --> 00:29:57,699
And you see it through a charmed medium.

480
00:29:58,639 --> 00:30:03,980
You cannot discern that the gilding is slime and the silk draperies cobwebs that

481
00:30:03,980 --> 00:30:10,080
the marble is sorted slate and the polished woods mere refuse chips and scaly bark.

482
00:30:10,260 --> 00:30:14,260
Now here, he pointed to the leafy enclosure we had entered.

483
00:30:15,339 --> 00:30:18,839
All is real, sweet and pure.

484
00:30:20,400 --> 00:30:25,699
He strayed down a walk edged with box, with apple trees, pear trees and cherry

485
00:30:25,701 --> 00:30:29,879
trees on one side, and a border on the other full of all sorts of old fashioned

486
00:30:29,881 --> 00:30:36,379
flowers, stocks, sweet willyums, primrosees, pansies, mingled with southern

487
00:30:36,381 --> 00:30:40,319
wood, sweet briar and various fragrant herbs.

488
00:30:41,500 --> 00:30:45,940
They were fresh now as a succession of april showers and

489
00:30:45,942 --> 00:30:50,040
gleams, followed by a lovely spring morning, could make them.

490
00:30:50,879 --> 00:30:56,440
The sun was just entering the east, and his light illumined the wreaths and

491
00:30:56,440 --> 00:31:01,139
dewy orchard trees and shone down the quiet walks under them.

492
00:31:02,180 --> 00:31:03,900
Jane, will you have a flower?

493
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:10,620
He gathered a half-blown rose, the first on the bush, and offered it to me.

494
00:31:10,819 --> 00:31:11,819
Thank you, sir.

495
00:31:12,699 --> 00:31:14,180
Do you like this sunrise, Jane?

496
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:18,779
That sky with its high and light clouds which are short and melt away as the day

497
00:31:18,781 --> 00:31:22,400
waxes warm, this placid and bombly atmosphere?

498
00:31:23,019 --> 00:31:25,339
I do, very much.

499
00:31:26,180 --> 00:31:28,580
You have passed a strange night, Jane.

500
00:31:29,779 --> 00:31:30,779
Yes, sir.

501
00:31:31,639 --> 00:31:33,019
And it has made you look pale.

502
00:31:33,900 --> 00:31:35,860
Were you afraid when I left you alone with Mason?

503
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:39,459
I was afraid of someone coming out of the inner room.

504
00:31:41,160 --> 00:31:42,900
But I had fastened the door.

505
00:31:43,639 --> 00:31:44,879
I had the key in my pocket.

506
00:31:45,739 --> 00:31:49,800
I should have been a careless shepherd if I had left a lamb, my pet lamb,

507
00:31:50,319 --> 00:31:53,819
so near a wolf's den, unguarded, you were safe.

508
00:31:55,620 --> 00:31:57,800
Will Grace pull live here still, sir?

509
00:31:59,180 --> 00:32:00,180
Oh, yes.

510
00:32:00,620 --> 00:32:01,980
Don't trouble your head about her.

511
00:32:02,559 --> 00:32:03,959
Put the thing out of your thoughts.

512
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:08,739
Yet it seems to me your life is hardly secure while she stays.

513
00:32:09,819 --> 00:32:10,819
Never fear.

514
00:32:11,199 --> 00:32:12,639
I will take care of myself.

515
00:32:14,300 --> 00:32:17,040
Is the danger you apprehended last night gone by now?

516
00:32:17,080 --> 00:32:24,379
Sir, I cannot vouch for that till Mason is out of England, nor even then.

517
00:32:25,440 --> 00:32:29,406
To live, for me, Jane, is to stand on a crater

518
00:32:29,408 --> 00:32:33,601
crust which may crack and spew fire any day.

519
00:32:34,400 --> 00:32:37,480
But Mr. Mason seems a man easily led.

520
00:32:38,440 --> 00:32:41,959
Your influence, sir, is evidently potent with him.

521
00:32:42,680 --> 00:32:45,900
He will never set you at defiance or willfully injure you.

522
00:32:46,680 --> 00:32:51,699
Oh, no, Mason will not defy me, nor knowing it will he hurt me.

523
00:32:52,959 --> 00:32:55,720
But unintentionally, he might in a moment.

524
00:32:56,459 --> 00:33:01,660
By one careless word deprive me if not of life, yet forever of happiness.

525
00:33:03,180 --> 00:33:04,940
Tell him to be cautious, sir.

526
00:33:05,739 --> 00:33:09,639
Let him know what you fear and show him how to hurt the danger.

527
00:33:10,620 --> 00:33:16,260
He laughed sadonically, hastily took my hand and has hastily threw it from him.

528
00:33:17,599 --> 00:33:23,800
If I could do that, Simpleton, where would the danger be, annihilated in a moment?

529
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:28,980
Ever since I have known Mason, I have only had to say to him, do that.

530
00:33:29,120 --> 00:33:31,339
And the thing has been done.

531
00:33:32,339 --> 00:33:34,279
But I cannot give him orders in this case.

532
00:33:35,059 --> 00:33:40,220
I cannot say beware of harming me, Richard, for it is imperative that I

533
00:33:40,220 --> 00:33:43,559
should keep him ignorant, that harm to me is possible.

534
00:33:44,900 --> 00:33:48,400
Now you look puzzled, and I will puzzle you further.

535
00:33:49,279 --> 00:33:51,319
You are my little friend, are you not?

536
00:33:52,559 --> 00:33:56,980
I like to serve you, sir, and to obey you in all that is right.

537
00:33:58,300 --> 00:33:59,959
Precisely, I see you do.

538
00:34:00,760 --> 00:34:06,519
I see genuine contentment in your gate and mean, your eye and face when you are

539
00:34:06,521 --> 00:34:10,521
helping me and pleasing me, working for me and with me,

540
00:34:10,521 --> 00:34:15,319
in, as you characteristically say, all that is right.

541
00:34:16,400 --> 00:34:20,900
For if I bid you do what you thought wrong, there would be no light-footed

542
00:34:20,900 --> 00:34:26,620
running, no neat-handed alacrity, no lively glance and animated complexion.

543
00:34:27,379 --> 00:34:31,819
My friend would then turn to me, quiet and pale and would say, no,

544
00:34:31,980 --> 00:34:33,559
sir, that is impossible.

545
00:34:33,561 --> 00:34:41,000
I cannot do it, because it is wrong, and would become immutable as a fixed star.

546
00:34:41,180 --> 00:34:48,220
Well, you too have power over me and may injure me, yet I dare not show you where I

547
00:34:48,220 --> 00:34:51,440
am vulnerable, lest, faithful and friendly

548
00:34:51,442 --> 00:34:55,800
as you are, you should trans-fix me at once.

549
00:34:56,680 --> 00:34:58,862
If you have no more to fear from Mr Mason

550
00:34:58,862 --> 00:35:02,580
than you have from me, sir, you are very safe.

551
00:35:03,559 --> 00:35:06,400
God grant it may be so, here Jane is an arbor, sit down.

552
00:35:07,680 --> 00:35:11,040
The arbor was an arch in the wall, lined with ivy.

553
00:35:11,819 --> 00:35:13,160
It contained a rustic seat.

554
00:35:14,239 --> 00:35:19,639
Mr. Rochester took it, leaving room, however, for me, but I stood before him.

555
00:35:20,419 --> 00:35:21,540
Sit, he said.

556
00:35:22,239 --> 00:35:23,580
The bench is long enough for two.

557
00:35:24,500 --> 00:35:27,279
You don't hesitate to take a place at my side, do you?

558
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:29,000
Is that wrong, Jane?

559
00:35:30,019 --> 00:35:35,160
I answered him by assuming it, to refuse would I felt have been unwise.

560
00:35:36,500 --> 00:35:42,559
Now, my little friend, while the sun drinks the dew, while all the flowers in

561
00:35:42,561 --> 00:35:46,959
this old garden awake can expand, and the birds fetch their young ones

562
00:35:46,961 --> 00:35:52,701
breakfast out of the thornfield, and the early bees do their first spell of work.

563
00:35:52,940 --> 00:35:56,660
I'll put a case to you which you must endeavour to suppose your own.

564
00:35:57,620 --> 00:36:02,065
But first, look at me and tell me you are at ease and not

565
00:36:02,065 --> 00:36:05,980
fearing that I err in detaining you, or that you err in staying.

566
00:36:07,319 --> 00:36:08,319
No, sir.

567
00:36:08,839 --> 00:36:09,839
I am content.

568
00:36:10,839 --> 00:36:11,839
Well then, Jane.

569
00:36:12,400 --> 00:36:13,680
Call to aid your fancy.

570
00:36:14,480 --> 00:36:17,692
Suppose you are no longer a girl well -reared and

571
00:36:17,694 --> 00:36:21,959
disciplined, but a wild boy indulged from childhood upwards.

572
00:36:22,959 --> 00:36:26,040
Imagine yourself in a remote foreign land.

573
00:36:26,760 --> 00:36:32,180
Conceive that you there commit a capital error, no matter of what nature or from

574
00:36:32,180 --> 00:36:36,383
what motives, but one whose consequences must follow

575
00:36:36,383 --> 00:36:39,720
you through life and taint all your existence.

576
00:36:40,660 --> 00:36:43,139
Mind, I don't say a crime.

577
00:36:44,239 --> 00:36:47,302
I'm not speaking of shedding of blood or any other guilty

578
00:36:47,302 --> 00:36:50,620
act, which might make the perpetrator amenable to the law.

579
00:36:51,760 --> 00:36:53,080
My word is error.

580
00:36:54,099 --> 00:36:58,500
The results of what you have done become in time to you utterly insupportable.

581
00:36:59,260 --> 00:37:01,239
You take measures to obtain relief.

582
00:37:02,040 --> 00:37:05,699
Unusual measures, but neither unlawful nor culpable.

583
00:37:06,800 --> 00:37:08,199
Still, you are miserable.

584
00:37:09,199 --> 00:37:12,400
For hope has quitted you on the very confines of life.

585
00:37:13,239 --> 00:37:16,571
Your son at noon darkens in an eclipse, which you

586
00:37:16,572 --> 00:37:19,641
feel will not leave it till the time of setting.

587
00:37:20,620 --> 00:37:25,339
Bitter and base associations have become the sole food of your memory.

588
00:37:26,139 --> 00:37:31,779
You wander here and there, seeking rest in exile, happiness in pleasure.

589
00:37:32,459 --> 00:37:38,099
I mean in heartless sensual pleasure, such as dulls intellect and blights

590
00:37:38,101 --> 00:37:41,125
feeling, heart weary and soul withered, you

591
00:37:41,125 --> 00:37:44,641
come home after years of voluntary banishment.

592
00:37:45,059 --> 00:37:47,080
You make a new acquaintance.

593
00:37:47,680 --> 00:37:49,220
How or where no matter.

594
00:37:50,080 --> 00:37:53,769
You find in this stranger much of the good and bright qualities

595
00:37:53,771 --> 00:37:58,819
which you have sought for 20 years and never before encountered.

596
00:37:59,559 --> 00:38:04,419
And they are all fresh, healthy, without soil and without taint.

597
00:38:05,199 --> 00:38:07,480
Such society revives, regenerates.

598
00:38:08,279 --> 00:38:13,160
You feel better, days come back, higher wishes, pureer feelings.

599
00:38:14,059 --> 00:38:17,767
You desire to recommence your life and to spend what remains

600
00:38:17,769 --> 00:38:21,260
to you of days in a way more worthy of an immortal being.

601
00:38:22,639 --> 00:38:27,940
To attain this end, are you justified in overleaping an obstacle of custom,

602
00:38:28,720 --> 00:38:33,239
a mere conventional impediment which neither your conscience sanctifies,

603
00:38:33,940 --> 00:38:35,540
nor your judgment approves?

604
00:38:36,160 --> 00:38:37,900
He paused for an answer.

605
00:38:38,819 --> 00:38:39,959
And what was I to say?

606
00:38:40,779 --> 00:38:45,480
Oh, for some good spirit to suggest a judicious and satisfactory response,

607
00:38:46,599 --> 00:38:47,599
vain aspiration.

608
00:38:48,819 --> 00:38:52,074
The West wind whispered in the ivy round me, but no

609
00:38:52,076 --> 00:38:55,459
gentle aerial borrowed its breath as a medium of speech.

610
00:38:56,220 --> 00:39:01,160
The birds sang in the treetops, but their song, however sweet,

611
00:39:01,680 --> 00:39:03,120
was inarticulate.

612
00:39:04,120 --> 00:39:07,860
Again, Mr. Rochester propounded his query.

613
00:39:09,230 --> 00:39:15,860
Is the wandering and sinful, but now rest -seeking and repentant, man justified in

614
00:39:15,860 --> 00:39:20,779
daring the world's opinion in order to attach to him forever this gentle,

615
00:39:21,040 --> 00:39:23,964
gracious, genial stranger thereby securing his

616
00:39:23,966 --> 00:39:27,781
own peace of mind and regeneration of life.

617
00:39:28,819 --> 00:39:30,620
Sir, I answered.

618
00:39:31,620 --> 00:39:34,330
A wanderer's repose or a sinner's reformation

619
00:39:34,332 --> 00:39:36,781
should never depend on a fellow -creature.

620
00:39:37,220 --> 00:39:42,800
Men and women die, philosophers falter in wisdom and Christians in goodness.

621
00:39:43,940 --> 00:39:47,995
If anyone you know has suffered an urge, let him look higher

622
00:39:47,997 --> 00:39:51,819
than his equals for strength to amend and solace to heal.

623
00:39:53,220 --> 00:39:59,821
But the instrument, the instrument, God who does the work, ordains the instrument.

624
00:40:00,260 --> 00:40:06,000
I have myself, I tell it you without parable, been a worldly, dissipated,

625
00:40:06,160 --> 00:40:11,239
restless man, and I believe I have found the instrument for my cure-in.

626
00:40:12,080 --> 00:40:13,080
He paused.

627
00:40:13,480 --> 00:40:17,900
The birds went on caroling, the leaves lightly rustling.

628
00:40:18,980 --> 00:40:23,699
I almost wondered they did not check their songs and whispers to catch the suspended

629
00:40:23,701 --> 00:40:26,410
revelation, but they would have had to wait

630
00:40:26,411 --> 00:40:29,860
many minutes so long was the silence protracted.

631
00:40:30,639 --> 00:40:33,940
At last, I looked up at the tardy speaker.

632
00:40:35,160 --> 00:40:36,699
He was looking eagerly at me.

633
00:40:38,379 --> 00:40:44,199
Little friend said he, in quite a change -tone, while his face changed too,

634
00:40:45,019 --> 00:40:49,919
losing all its softness and gravity and becoming harsh and sarcastic.

635
00:40:50,500 --> 00:40:54,360
You have noticed my tender pinchant for Miss Ingram.

636
00:40:55,120 --> 00:41:00,599
Don't you think, if I married her, she would regenerate me with a vengeance?

637
00:41:01,480 --> 00:41:04,714
He got up instantly, went quite to the other end of

638
00:41:04,716 --> 00:41:07,980
the walk, and when he came back, he was humming a tune.

639
00:41:09,220 --> 00:41:12,940
Jane, Jane said he, stopping before me.

640
00:41:13,919 --> 00:41:15,660
You are quite pale with your vigils.

641
00:41:23,279 --> 00:41:24,980
Don't you conformation of the word?

642
00:41:25,639 --> 00:41:26,779
What cold fingers.

643
00:41:27,699 --> 00:41:32,241
They were warmer last night when I touched them at the door of the mysterious chamber.

644
00:41:32,639 --> 00:41:34,919
Jane, when will you watch with me again?

645
00:41:36,379 --> 00:41:37,980
Whenever I can be useful, sir.

646
00:41:39,180 --> 00:41:45,461
For instance, the night before I am married, I am sure I shall not be able to sleep.

647
00:41:45,660 --> 00:41:48,059
Will you promise to sit up with me to bear me company?

648
00:41:48,900 --> 00:41:51,080
To you, I can talk of my lovely one.

649
00:41:51,699 --> 00:41:54,239
For now you have seen her and know her.

650
00:41:55,139 --> 00:41:56,139
Yes, sir.

651
00:41:57,000 --> 00:41:58,000
She's a rare one.

652
00:41:58,260 --> 00:41:59,260
Is she not, Jane?

653
00:41:59,959 --> 00:42:00,959
Yes, sir.

654
00:42:01,720 --> 00:42:02,720
A strapper.

655
00:42:03,059 --> 00:42:04,739
A real strapper, Jane.

656
00:42:05,239 --> 00:42:09,779
Big brown and boxum, with hair just such as the ladies of Carthage must have had.

657
00:42:10,300 --> 00:42:11,300
Bless me.

658
00:42:11,419 --> 00:42:13,160
There's Denton Lynn in the stables.

659
00:42:14,059 --> 00:42:16,120
Go in by the shrubbery through that wicked.

660
00:42:17,180 --> 00:42:23,680
As I went one way, he went another, and I heard him in the yard, saying cheerfully.

661
00:42:24,760 --> 00:42:27,400
Mason got the start of you all this morning.

662
00:42:28,040 --> 00:42:29,400
He was gone before sunrise.

663
00:42:29,959 --> 00:42:31,559
I rose at four to see him off.
